# Generated from: specs/503-fix-duplicate-changelog-entry-when-delivery-rolls-a-hand-written-issue-entry/requirements.md
Feature: Delivery does not duplicate the issue's CHANGELOG entry

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: AC1 hand-written issue entry is rolled without a generated duplicate
    Given the Unreleased section contains "### Fixed" with the bullet "- Corrected delivery (#42)."
    When prepare-version runs for issue 42
    Then the new version section contains that bullet once
    And the new version section contains no generated "### Changed" line for issue 42
    And the Unreleased section is empty

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: AC2 generated entry is added when no entry references the issue
    Given the Unreleased section is empty or contains only bullets without "(#42)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue 42
    Then the new version section ends with "### Changed" and "- Deliver verified changes (#42)"

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: AC3 approved breaking change keeps the BREAKING category
    Given issue 42 declares BREAKING with an approved major version bump
    And no Unreleased bullet contains "(#42)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue 42
    Then the version is bumped to the next major
    And the generated line is under "### Changed (BREAKING)"

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: AC4 re-run after rolling a hand-written entry does not bump again
    Given prepare-version already rolled a hand-written "(#42)" entry into the new version and committed it
    When prepare-version runs again for issue 42
    Then VERSION, package.json, and CHANGELOG.md are unchanged and no commit is created
    And delivery does not fail with "version_not_prepared"

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: AC5 matching is exact to the issue number
    Given the Unreleased section contains bullets with "(#4)" and "(#420)" but none with "(#42)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue 42
    Then the generated line "- Deliver verified changes (#42)" is added
